Negative control for the refinements riding the display row (`R6-16`).

Drops the chips and Clear all off the display row, which is what put them back on
a standalone row of their own above Results — the layout `R6-16` supersedes `G5`
to remove. One row: Results · count · chips · Clear all on the left, sort and the
view toggle on the right.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the display-row spec — the row carries the active refinements after its
count, and no second row carries them.

